1
00:00:03,921 --> 00:00:05,213
( blowing noisemakers )

2
00:00:05,255 --> 00:00:06,632
ALL:
Happy Birthday!

3
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:11,804
Come on.
Rach, come on.

4
00:00:11,846 --> 00:00:13,054
Rach...
It's your birthday.

5
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:15,432
Hey.

6
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:17,434
She's not as pretty

7
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:20,729
as she was
when she was 29.

8
00:00:20,771 --> 00:00:23,524
Miss Green would like
to establish some ground rules

9
00:00:23,565 --> 00:00:25,526
before she comes out.

10
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:27,110
She would appreciate it

11
00:00:27,152 --> 00:00:29,780
if you didn't use the words
"old" or "downhill"

12
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:31,740
or "they still look
pretty damn good."

13
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,120
They do!

14
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:39,122
Rachel...

15
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:41,208
come on out!

16
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:42,292
Monica made
breakfast.

17
00:00:42,334 --> 00:00:43,919
Chocolate chip pancakes!

18
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:46,296
We've got presents.

19
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:50,300
Good ones?

20
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:52,260
They all came from the list

21
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:54,722
you handed out to us
two weeks ago.

22
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:59,351
Well, can I keep the presents
and still be 29?

23
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:00,728
Come on, Rach.

24
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:03,022
Look, turning 30's
not that big a deal.

25
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:04,398
Oh, really?

26
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:06,066
Is that how you felt
when you turned 30?

27
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:08,235
Why, God, why?

28
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:10,029
We had a deal.

29
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:13,032
Let the others grow old, not me.

30
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:15,576
( sobbing )

31
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:17,786
Oh, come on, you guys,
is it just me?

32
00:01:17,828 --> 00:01:19,371
Am I overreacting to this?

33
00:01:19,413 --> 00:01:21,248
No, Rach, it's not just you.

34
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:23,542
My 30th birthday certainly
wasn't that much fun.

35
00:01:23,584 --> 00:01:26,045
And now
Chandler.

36
00:01:26,085 --> 00:01:29,757
We're all
getting so old.

37
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:32,801
Why are you
doing this
to us?

38
00:01:41,894 --> 00:01:46,231
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

39
00:01:46,273 --> 00:01:48,275
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

40
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:51,403
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

41
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:56,116
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

42
00:01:56,157 --> 00:01:59,453
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

43
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:01,747
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

44
00:02:01,789 --> 00:02:05,084
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

45
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:11,590
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

46
00:02:15,135 --> 00:02:17,429
Rach, you're in
a great place
in your life.

47
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:19,556
You have an
amazing job,
good friends.

48
00:02:19,598 --> 00:02:20,766
Yeah.

49
00:02:20,808 --> 00:02:22,601
Your roommate's
a soap opera star.

50
00:02:22,643 --> 00:02:24,645
Your character's in a coma.

51
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:27,898
I promised myself

52
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:29,900
I wasn't going to cry
at this one.

53
00:02:29,942 --> 00:02:31,276
RACHEL:
Look, you know

54
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:32,945
I know my life's
going pretty well

55
00:02:32,987 --> 00:02:34,488
but I look around
and I just see

56
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:36,323
so many people
who have accomplished

57
00:02:36,364 --> 00:02:38,617
so many of their goals
by the time they're 30.

58
00:02:38,659 --> 00:02:42,203
Yeah, but you shouldn't
compare yourself to me.

59
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:43,538
Come on, Phoebe!

60
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,290
You can do it,
Phoebe!

61
00:02:45,332 --> 00:02:46,500
Come on,
Phoebe,
come on.

62
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:47,501
There you go!

63
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:49,210
( cheering )

64
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:52,171
Yay!
Yay!
Whoo-hoo!

65
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:53,172
There you go.

66
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:54,967
I did it!

67
00:02:55,009 --> 00:02:57,094
Look, one mile on a hippity-hop.

68
00:02:57,136 --> 00:02:58,595
Ha-ha! That's it.

69
00:02:58,637 --> 00:03:01,348
That's everything I wanted to do
before I was 30.

70
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:04,351
Oh! Except I wanted to patch
things up with my sister.

71
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:05,602
Oh, well, but... yay!

72
00:03:05,644 --> 00:03:06,937
( cheering )

73
00:03:06,979 --> 00:03:08,396
PHOEBE:
And-and girls--

74
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:09,898
this thing
is a godsend

75
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,274
if you know
what I mean.

76
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:14,987
( whooping )

77
00:03:15,029 --> 00:03:16,321
Whoo.

78
00:03:16,363 --> 00:03:17,698
Whoo.

79
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,995
Come on, let's have
some fun, huh?

80
00:03:23,037 --> 00:03:24,287
What do you want to do today?

81
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,205
Nothing. I don't want
to do anything.

82
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:27,833
Doing nothing on your 30th

83
00:03:27,875 --> 00:03:29,835
is better than
doing something stupid...

84
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:31,378
like Ross.

85
00:03:31,419 --> 00:03:34,715
Hey, that was
a practical purchase.

86
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:38,218
I needed that car
for transportation, okay?

87
00:03:38,259 --> 00:03:40,054
I-I have a child.

88
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:43,724
How hot do I look in this,huh?

89
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:45,059
Ross,
a sports car?

90
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:47,186
Wouldn't it have
been cheaper

91
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:49,604
to just stuff a sock
down there?

92
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:52,941
That's not what this
is about, okay?

93
00:03:52,983 --> 00:03:54,943
I-I am a sports
car enthusiast.

94
00:03:54,985 --> 00:03:56,444
I've always
been into cars.

95
00:03:56,486 --> 00:03:57,612
Hey, what's...

96
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:58,989
the horsepower
on this thing?

97
00:03:59,031 --> 00:04:01,783
I don't know,
but-but look how shiny.

98
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:06,413
I can't believe
you bought this.

99
00:04:06,454 --> 00:04:07,998
Hey, could I have a ride, stud?

100
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,666
Hop in.

101
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:14,504
Get ready for
the smoothest
ride of your life.

102
00:04:14,546 --> 00:04:15,923
( engine revving )

103
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:30,771
( tires squeaking )

104
00:04:38,319 --> 00:04:40,239
Damn it!

105
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:43,742
Okay, who's next?

106
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:48,080
You know what?

107
00:04:48,122 --> 00:04:49,372
I am going to do
something today.

108
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:50,874
I'm not just
going to sit around

109
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:52,375
like some old lady.

110
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:54,044
I'm going to get
something pierced... mm-hmm.

111
00:04:54,086 --> 00:04:55,462
Like my, uh...

112
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,589
like my nose or my tongue,
or something.

113
00:04:57,631 --> 00:04:59,507
Really? 'Cause, you know,
that hurts.

114
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:01,843
So what? You know what,
the way I see it...

115
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:03,344
Ow! Son of a bitch!

116
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:06,473
TAG:
Look, Rachel.

117
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:08,225
I know what
you're going through.

118
00:05:08,267 --> 00:05:11,311
I'm totally freaked out
about turning 25.

119
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:16,650
Get out... get out
of my apartment.

120
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:18,485
MONICA:
All right, Rach,
for what it's worth

121
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:20,320
I think that you're doing great.

122
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:21,989
I mean, you know, let's face it.

123
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,157
No one handles this well.

124
00:05:23,198 --> 00:05:24,699
Hmm, least
of all you.

125
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:25,742
Hmm.

126
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:30,705
JOEY:
Ah...

127
00:05:30,747 --> 00:05:32,082
Would you put
that back on?

128
00:05:32,124 --> 00:05:33,667
Monica's going to be here
any minute.

129
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:36,003
But it hurts
my Joey's apple.

130
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:39,881
Okay, for the last time--

131
00:05:39,923 --> 00:05:43,260
it's not named after
each individual man.

132
00:05:46,847 --> 00:05:49,641
You've done a
wonderful job with
this party, Chandler.

133
00:05:49,683 --> 00:05:51,059
Everything looks
so lovely.

134
00:05:51,101 --> 00:05:53,436
Oh, well, not
as lovely as you.

135
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:54,771
I mean, I can't believe

136
00:05:54,813 --> 00:05:56,606
that you would have
a 30-year-old daughter.

137
00:05:56,648 --> 00:05:58,942
And you, I can't believe
that you would have

138
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:00,527
a tux that's
30 years old.

139
00:06:00,568 --> 00:06:02,529
It's older than that.

140
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:04,865
Ross was actually conceived
right near this tuxedo.

141
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:06,908
Oh.

142
00:06:08,743 --> 00:06:10,996
Okay, everybody hide.
I saw her; she's coming.

143
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:12,080
Okay, okay.

144
00:06:12,122 --> 00:06:13,372
Everybody down.
Everybody down!

145
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:16,751
( loud fumbling noise )

146
00:06:18,377 --> 00:06:19,338
( noise ceases )

147
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:20,755
Okay, everybody stay here.

148
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:22,632
I will find out what's going on.

149
00:06:24,134 --> 00:06:25,677
Hey!

150
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:29,348
You got the door open!

151
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:31,766
Hey-hey,
are you drunk?

152
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,227
No.

153
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:34,519
( laughs )

154
00:06:34,561 --> 00:06:36,271
Okay.

155
00:06:36,313 --> 00:06:37,564
Whoa!

156
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:40,067
Okay.

157
00:06:40,108 --> 00:06:41,568
Okay.

158
00:06:41,609 --> 00:06:43,570
See...

159
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:46,698
see, I wa... I was a little
nervous about turning...

160
00:06:46,740 --> 00:06:48,283
thirty.

161
00:06:48,325 --> 00:06:49,576
Huh.

162
00:06:49,617 --> 00:06:50,952
So, the busboys

163
00:06:50,994 --> 00:06:52,787
took me out
for some drinks.

164
00:06:56,083 --> 00:06:58,585
I'm going to puke
on you later.

165
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,755
Okay, here's the thing.

166
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:03,757
We have thrown
a very formal surprise party

167
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,092
for you in there.

168
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:06,760
All your friends
are in there

169
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:08,178
and your parents.

170
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,179
No!
Yes!

171
00:07:09,221 --> 00:07:10,513
Yes!
No!

172
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:13,392
Oh, no, my parents
have never seen me drunk.

173
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:14,601
That they know of.

174
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:16,270
Okay, here's the thing.

175
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:17,729
We're going to get
you some coffee

176
00:07:17,771 --> 00:07:19,773
and they will never
know that you're drunk.

177
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,066
Really? You promise?

178
00:07:21,108 --> 00:07:22,442
Yes. I'll take care of it.

179
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:24,694
Mmm, I love you
so much.

180
00:07:24,736 --> 00:07:26,238
Okay.

181
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:29,074
We have to do something
about your breath.

182
00:07:29,116 --> 00:07:32,286
What about
your breath?

183
00:07:32,327 --> 00:07:35,414
That's still
yours.

184
00:07:36,455 --> 00:07:38,625
Okay, now remember

185
00:07:38,666 --> 00:07:40,001
it's a surprise party

186
00:07:40,043 --> 00:07:42,587
so when you go in,
act surprised.

187
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:43,588
Okay.

188
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:44,923
Okay. Shh.
Ready?

189
00:07:44,965 --> 00:07:45,966
Shh.

190
00:07:52,306 --> 00:07:53,765
ALL:
Surprise!

191
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:55,850
( screaming )

192
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:01,648
Okay, forward, forward.

193
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:02,732
Stop!

194
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:06,069
Okay, back... stop!

195
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:09,489
Okay, forwa...

196
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:11,325
Stop, stop, stop!

197
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:13,534
Okay, okay, here's what
we're going to do, okay?

198
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:15,287
I'm going to break
into this mini-van

199
00:08:15,329 --> 00:08:16,788
and put it in neutral.

200
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,290
You guys push it forward

201
00:08:18,332 --> 00:08:20,792
so Ross can drive
out of the spot.

202
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:22,501
Okay.
Okay?

203
00:08:22,543 --> 00:08:23,878
All right, here we go.

204
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,260
( alarm sounding )

205
00:08:30,302 --> 00:08:32,387
Haul ass!

206
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:44,691
Happy 30th birthday.

207
00:08:44,732 --> 00:08:46,567
Here.

208
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:48,153
It's for the child in you.

209
00:08:48,195 --> 00:08:50,155
And the woman.

210
00:08:50,197 --> 00:08:51,656
Happy 30th.

211
00:08:51,698 --> 00:08:53,616
Right, why do you
keep saying that?

212
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:56,286
Because it's
our 30th birthday.

213
00:08:56,328 --> 00:08:58,330
Yeah, no. We're
not 30, we're 31.

214
00:08:58,372 --> 00:08:59,914
Okay.

215
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:01,624
Uh... wait!

216
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:05,753
Oh, it's you.

217
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:07,672
Yeah. What?

218
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:09,924
Yeah, we're
not 30, we're 31.

219
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,343
Nuh-uh!

220
00:09:11,385 --> 00:09:12,552
Yuh-huh! That's
what it says

221
00:09:12,593 --> 00:09:14,346
on my birth
certificate.

222
00:09:14,388 --> 00:09:15,972
You have your
birth certificate?

223
00:09:16,014 --> 00:09:17,932
Yeah. I got a big box
of family stuff

224
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:18,975
when my mom died.

225
00:09:19,017 --> 00:09:20,560
Our mom.

226
00:09:20,601 --> 00:09:23,188
Right. Okay.

227
00:09:23,230 --> 00:09:25,648
Do you have
my birth certificate?

228
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:28,193
No. I sold it
to a Swedish runaway.

229
00:09:28,235 --> 00:09:29,903
Okay.

230
00:09:31,071 --> 00:09:32,364
Oh, my God.

231
00:09:32,406 --> 00:09:35,700
Oh, my God,
we are 31.

232
00:09:35,742 --> 00:09:37,202
Yeah.

233
00:09:37,244 --> 00:09:41,039
I just lost a whole year
of my life.

234
00:09:41,081 --> 00:09:43,750
Okay.

235
00:09:43,791 --> 00:09:45,502
Your middle name is Pamela?

236
00:09:45,544 --> 00:09:46,503
Yes.

237
00:09:46,545 --> 00:09:48,547
Oh. I never knew mine.

238
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:49,839
Do you remember what it is?

239
00:09:49,881 --> 00:09:52,092
Yes. "Phoebe."

240
00:09:53,218 --> 00:09:54,719
That's my first name.

241
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:57,597
Right. Okay. Then, no.

242
00:09:59,766 --> 00:10:01,518
Okay, look at that--
we made it

243
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:02,769
all the way
across the room.

244
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:03,770
You're doing great.

245
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,272
What's going on?

246
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:07,148
Monica's
a little drunk.

247
00:10:07,190 --> 00:10:09,568
Yay! I love
drunk Monica.

248
00:10:09,608 --> 00:10:11,403
Shh.

249
00:10:11,445 --> 00:10:14,864
Oh, she's so much more fun
than regular Monica.

250
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:19,494
She doesn't
want her parents
to know she's drunk.

251
00:10:19,536 --> 00:10:20,912
Oh. All right,
all right.

252
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:22,414
Here's what we'll do.

253
00:10:22,456 --> 00:10:24,416
I'll get twice
as drunk as Monica

254
00:10:24,458 --> 00:10:26,918
and then no one's even
going to notice her.

255
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:31,339
What...

256
00:10:31,381 --> 00:10:32,507
What's going on?

257
00:10:32,549 --> 00:10:33,550
( sighs )

258
00:10:33,592 --> 00:10:35,135
Monica's wasted.

259
00:10:35,176 --> 00:10:38,430
Maybe that'll
liven up this party.

260
00:10:38,472 --> 00:10:41,057
Okay, will you just go help
her get changed, please?

261
00:10:41,099 --> 00:10:43,310
Okay, but taking care
of a drunk, naked woman

262
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:44,727
seems like a job
for Joey.

263
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:45,812
Yep.

264
00:10:48,856 --> 00:10:50,317
This one's
from me.

265
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:51,734
Ah!

266
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:53,236
It wasn't on your list,
but hopefully

267
00:10:53,278 --> 00:10:54,529
you'll think it's really fun.

268
00:10:55,572 --> 00:10:59,242
A scooter!

269
00:10:59,284 --> 00:11:02,954
Stick to the list.

270
00:11:02,996 --> 00:11:07,125
Always stick
to the list.

271
00:11:07,167 --> 00:11:08,960
No! No, no, I love it.
Thank you.

272
00:11:09,002 --> 00:11:10,462
CHANDLER:
Okay, open
ours next.

273
00:11:10,504 --> 00:11:11,670
Open ours next.

274
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:12,671
Okay.

275
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,132
Now that you're a couple

276
00:11:14,174 --> 00:11:15,467
we don't get two presents
from you guys?

277
00:11:15,509 --> 00:11:18,761
For my last birthday,
you gave me a hug.

278
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:20,763
Okay, read the card,
read the card.

279
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,849
Okay.

280
00:11:24,518 --> 00:11:27,854
"Happy Birthday, Grandma.

281
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:32,066
"It's better to be
over the hill...

282
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:33,318
Ah!

283
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:35,694
"than buried under it.

284
00:11:38,615 --> 00:11:40,659
"All our love,
Monica and Chandler."

285
00:11:40,699 --> 00:11:41,868
That's funny.

286
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:43,328
No, no, no, no...

287
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:44,496
That was a joke.

288
00:11:44,538 --> 00:11:46,039
No, I know, I get it.

289
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,582
It's funny.

290
00:11:47,624 --> 00:11:49,750
No, because you're not
a grandmother.

291
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:51,294
I know,
because to be a grandmother

292
00:11:51,336 --> 00:11:53,547
you have to be married
and have children

293
00:11:53,588 --> 00:11:55,923
and I don't have any
of those things.

294
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:58,593
That's why it's so funny.

295
00:11:58,635 --> 00:12:00,512
I'm just going to go...

296
00:12:00,554 --> 00:12:01,680
( choking up )

297
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,056
( door shuts )

298
00:12:04,558 --> 00:12:07,644
All you had to do
was buy the card.

299
00:12:13,692 --> 00:12:15,276
Okay, you know what?

300
00:12:15,318 --> 00:12:16,861
I realized it was stupid
to get upset

301
00:12:16,903 --> 00:12:18,405
about not having
a husband and kids.

302
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:21,241
All I really needed
was a plan.

303
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:23,117
See, I want to have three kids.

304
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,661
Well, let me guess--

305
00:12:24,703 --> 00:12:26,580
and you want to have them
all at the same time

306
00:12:26,621 --> 00:12:28,789
and you want to have them
for your brother.

307
00:12:28,831 --> 00:12:32,126
As I was saying...

308
00:12:32,168 --> 00:12:34,254
I should probably have
the first of the three kids

309
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:35,880
by the time I'm 35, right?

310
00:12:35,922 --> 00:12:38,007
Which gives me five years.

311
00:12:38,049 --> 00:12:39,634
Oh.

312
00:12:39,676 --> 00:12:41,595
So if I want to have a kid
when I'm 35

313
00:12:41,636 --> 00:12:43,680
I don't have to get pregnant
until I'm 34

314
00:12:43,722 --> 00:12:45,139
which gives Prada four years

315
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:46,974
to start making
maternity clothes.

316
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:51,104
Oh, wait, but...

317
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,606
now, I do want to be married
for a year

318
00:12:52,647 --> 00:12:53,690
before I get pregnant.

319
00:12:53,732 --> 00:12:55,400
Really! That long?

320
00:13:00,614 --> 00:13:03,157
Look all you want,
it's happening.

321
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:08,455
So I don't have to get married
until I'm 33.

322
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:10,665
That's three years!
That's three whole years!

323
00:13:10,707 --> 00:13:12,208
Oh, wait a minute, though--

324
00:13:12,250 --> 00:13:15,836
I'll need a year-and-a-half
to plan the wedding...

325
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:17,422
and I'd like to know the guy

326
00:13:17,464 --> 00:13:19,257
for, like, a year,
year-and-a-half

327
00:13:19,299 --> 00:13:22,427
before we get engaged...

328
00:13:22,469 --> 00:13:27,641
which means I need to meet
the guy by the time I'm 30...

329
00:13:27,682 --> 00:13:31,770
Which is fine,
because you just turned...

330
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:34,855
twenty-eight!

331
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:37,400
No, Ross, no!
It is not fine!

332
00:13:37,442 --> 00:13:39,026
According to my plan

333
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:40,945
I should already be with the guy
that I'm gonna marry!

334
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:42,656
TAG:
Woo-hoo!

335
00:13:42,697 --> 00:13:45,116
Mmm!

336
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:50,622
Will you quit hogging it!

337
00:13:54,793 --> 00:13:56,628
Oh, I'm telling you

338
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:58,672
it's like watching Bambi
learn how to walk.

339
00:14:00,632 --> 00:14:02,175
You're drunk.

340
00:14:02,216 --> 00:14:03,468
( both giggling )

341
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:06,805
Mom and Dad
are gonna be mad.

342
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:10,224
Maybe I'm a little drunk now.

343
00:14:11,850 --> 00:14:13,478
Hey, are those crab cakes?

344
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:14,729
Yeah.

345
00:14:14,771 --> 00:14:16,731
Did I not tell you
to come straight to me

346
00:14:16,773 --> 00:14:18,525
when more crab cakes
were ready?

347
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:20,276
Okay...

348
00:14:20,318 --> 00:14:21,861
How you feeling?

349
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:25,615
You are so handsome!

350
00:14:25,657 --> 00:14:27,325
Mmm!

351
00:14:27,367 --> 00:14:30,537
I want to make love to you
right here, right now!

352
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:31,954
( growls )

353
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:35,916
I really wish that you wouldn't.

354
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:38,419
Now all you have to do

355
00:14:38,461 --> 00:14:41,047
is just get through a
little bit more, okay?

356
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:43,049
Then we can put
you in bed, okay?

357
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:47,554
Just smile and don't
talk to anyone.

358
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:49,055
Speech! Speech!

359
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:51,558
Let's hear
from the birthday girl, huh?

360
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:53,685
Pheebs!

361
00:14:53,727 --> 00:14:56,103
You see, everybody's
looking at me.

362
00:14:56,145 --> 00:14:58,356
The plan's working.

363
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:02,068
I didn't even have to
take off my top yet.

364
00:15:02,109 --> 00:15:04,153
Speech!
Come on, Monica!

365
00:15:04,195 --> 00:15:05,946
CROWD:
Speech! Speech!

366
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:08,616
Hey, Chandler,
you can't

367
00:15:08,658 --> 00:15:10,910
keep your hands off her
for one second!

368
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:12,911
Oh, I think
it's nice.

369
00:15:12,953 --> 00:15:15,122
I think it's
necessary.

370
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:26,050
I-I-I want to thank you all
for coming--

371
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:29,429
my family and my friends.

372
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:30,971
Woo... hoo!

373
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:36,394
I'd really like to say
that I'm, um...

374
00:15:37,978 --> 00:15:41,691
you know what
I'd really like to say?

375
00:15:41,733 --> 00:15:44,151
I'm drunk!

376
00:15:46,613 --> 00:15:47,906
That's right, Mom and Dad

377
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:51,576
your little Harmomica
is hammered!

378
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:56,247
And guess what?
I've been drunk before.

379
00:15:56,289 --> 00:15:58,124
( laughing )

380
00:15:58,165 --> 00:16:00,167
And I've smoked a cigarette.

381
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:02,253
But you know what?
You know what?

382
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:04,964
( laughing ):
It's all okay.

383
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:08,843
It's okay
because I turned 30 today

384
00:16:08,885 --> 00:16:11,471
and I can do anything I want...

385
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:12,806
( laughing )

386
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:16,225
because I... am a grown-up.

387
00:16:20,772 --> 00:16:22,982
Oh, quick...
quick, help me get this off.

388
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:24,692
Yeah!

389
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:29,823
I lost a whole year!

390
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:32,659
I can believe it!
This is so unfair!

391
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,828
Come on, Pheebs,
it'll be okay.

392
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:36,329
Will it? Will it?

393
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:38,539
How would you feel

394
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:40,333
if you found out you were 31?

395
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:41,960
That's not gonna happen-- no--

396
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:44,378
because we have a new deal.

397
00:16:45,964 --> 00:16:47,841
Plus, it totally ruined
my schedule.

398
00:16:47,882 --> 00:16:50,343
I haven't done any of the things
I wanted to do

399
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:52,136
by the time I was 31.

400
00:16:52,178 --> 00:16:53,137
Like what?

401
00:16:53,179 --> 00:16:54,555
Like, okay, I-I...

402
00:16:54,597 --> 00:16:56,683
I haven't met
any Portuguese people

403
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:59,686
I... I haven't had
the perfect kiss

404
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,980
and I haven't been
to sniper school.

405
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:05,065
Phoebe, you know what?

406
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:07,151
Why don't we just go upstairs
and have some birthday cake.

407
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:09,779
No, I just feel like being
by myself for awhile, all right?

408
00:17:09,821 --> 00:17:11,614
I'll see you guys later. Thanks.

409
00:17:13,199 --> 00:17:15,535
Oh, poor Pheebs.

410
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:17,119
Hey, you know what,
you guys?

411
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:19,288
I think I'm going
to go walk her home.

412
00:17:19,330 --> 00:17:20,832
Okay.

413
00:17:22,333 --> 00:17:24,293
Oh, man!

414
00:17:24,335 --> 00:17:25,294
What?

415
00:17:25,336 --> 00:17:28,297
He's gonna eat the cake!

416
00:17:28,339 --> 00:17:30,008
Pheebs!

417
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:31,009
Wait up.

418
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:32,468
Listen, uh...

419
00:17:32,510 --> 00:17:34,512
Close your eyes.

420
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:50,110
Maybe that's one thing
you can cross off your list.

421
00:17:51,988 --> 00:17:54,407
Oh, yeah.

422
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:57,994
Oh, and plus,
I'm one-sixteenth Portuguese.

423
00:17:58,036 --> 00:17:59,037
Oh!

424
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:04,792
Okay, is everybody clear?

425
00:18:04,834 --> 00:18:06,836
We're gonna pick it up...

426
00:18:08,963 --> 00:18:10,506
and move it.

427
00:18:11,549 --> 00:18:13,384
Now, all we need
is teamwork, okay?

428
00:18:13,426 --> 00:18:16,971
We're gonna lift
the car...

429
00:18:17,013 --> 00:18:20,266
and slide it out.

430
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:23,227
Lift...

431
00:18:23,269 --> 00:18:25,730
and slide.

432
00:18:25,772 --> 00:18:27,023
Ross, I really
don't think--

433
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:29,483
Lift...

434
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:32,070
and slide.

435
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:33,487
Okay, here we go.

436
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:34,864
ROSS:
All right, everyone--

437
00:18:34,906 --> 00:18:36,908
Lift...

438
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:42,580
and slide!

439
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,585
Hey, Joey...

440
00:18:47,627 --> 00:18:50,170
Aw, come on, Rach,
my turn just started!

441
00:18:51,589 --> 00:18:54,050
Actually, I just want
to talk to Tag.

442
00:18:54,092 --> 00:18:55,175
Oh. Okay.

443
00:18:55,217 --> 00:18:57,219
Hey! Can I ride this outside?

444
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:58,763
Whatever, okay?
I'm not your mother.

445
00:19:00,347 --> 00:19:01,390
Not in the street!

446
00:19:01,432 --> 00:19:02,433
Yeah!

447
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:05,728
Hi. Hi.
Hey.

448
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:07,438
How you doing?
You feeling any better?

449
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:10,566
Yeah, I'm doing okay.
I'm... um...

450
00:19:10,608 --> 00:19:12,110
Let's talk.

451
00:19:12,150 --> 00:19:13,778
Okay.

452
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:14,862
Um...

453
00:19:14,904 --> 00:19:16,614
What's up?

454
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:19,241
Uh... Tag, um...

455
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:21,077
you're such a great guy

456
00:19:21,119 --> 00:19:23,579
and we have so much fun
together, but I don...

457
00:19:23,621 --> 00:19:24,705
Wait...

458
00:19:24,747 --> 00:19:27,708
I think I see
where you're going.

459
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:30,628
But before you say
anything else, can I just
say one more thing?

460
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:41,430
Well said...

461
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:46,936
and a good example of the fun
I was referring to...

462
00:19:46,978 --> 00:19:49,022
Uh... but...

463
00:19:49,063 --> 00:19:50,314
( nervous chuckle )

464
00:19:50,356 --> 00:19:51,983
I just think
I'm past the point

465
00:19:52,025 --> 00:19:54,027
where I can, you know,
just have fun.

466
00:19:54,068 --> 00:19:55,235
Rachel, don't do this.

467
00:19:55,277 --> 00:19:57,196
This is just because
you're turning 30.

468
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:59,365
Yeah, it is.

469
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:01,034
But you're just a kid.

470
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:03,119
I mean, you're...
you're 25.

471
00:20:03,161 --> 00:20:04,370
24, actually.

472
00:20:04,411 --> 00:20:05,913
Oh, God.

473
00:20:08,332 --> 00:20:09,542
You know what I wish?

474
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:13,295
I wish you were
six years older.

475
00:20:13,337 --> 00:20:15,548
Well, actually,
if I'm wishing for stuff

476
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:17,884
I actually wish
I was six years younger.

477
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:19,969
Me, too.

478
00:20:20,011 --> 00:20:21,846
Yeah. I'm sorry.

479
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:32,065
Hey. How'd it go?

480
00:20:32,106 --> 00:20:35,317
Oh... if I only want two kids

481
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:37,695
can I keep him for another year?

482
00:20:39,113 --> 00:20:40,781
You did
the right thing.

483
00:20:44,202 --> 00:20:45,870
( groans )

484
00:20:45,912 --> 00:20:47,914
I don't like this anymore.

485
00:20:52,376 --> 00:20:56,296
Well, here we are, just
a bunch of 30-year-olds.

486
00:20:56,338 --> 00:21:01,135
Do you realize,
in ten years, we're
going to be 40?

487
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,640
Why, God?

488
00:21:06,682 --> 00:21:09,643
Why are you
doing this to us?

489
00:21:17,944 --> 00:21:21,321
Yes! My baby's
finally free!

490
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:23,116
All right!

491
00:21:23,157 --> 00:21:25,659
Start it up!
Let's go!

492
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:27,203
( engine starts )

493
00:21:27,245 --> 00:21:28,913
Hoo-hoo!

494
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,586
How hot are we?

495
00:21:40,967 --> 00:21:43,219
( turns off engine )

496
00:21:43,261 --> 00:21:45,263
You want to buy a car?

